  "description": "NACA 0012, chord 0.3 m, Re_c = 4e5, tripped.  Measured suction-side boundary layer near the trailing edge: delta* = 2.25 mm, C_f = 0.0024, dp/dx = 181.87 Pa/m (Table 3.1).  The thesis compares the wall-pressure models with the measured surface-pressure spectrum (Fig. 3.6): see the wall-pressure panel of the self-noise tab.  Expected (thesis p. 93): Rozenberg's model (eq. 3.27) gives the best spectral shape; Kim-George agrees at low frequency but over-predicts the mid and high frequencies; Amiet and Chase-Howe under-predict the low and over-predict the high frequencies.  The far-field span (0.4 m) and observer (1.2 m) are illustrative.",
